尽管他从警察局退休已久，但申纳一直对维也纳森林发现女性的新闻着迷。这让他想起了一起他从未能放下的案件，即1973年在萨尔茨堡发生的玛丽卡·霍瓦特（Marika Horvat）谋杀案。后来，当杰克·翁特韦格被指控杀害玛格丽特·沙弗（Margaret Schaffer）时，奥古斯特·申纳确信他也谋杀了玛丽卡。他从未有足够的证据起诉他，但看到自己的嫌疑人被判无期徒刑，他感到有些安慰。现在，将近二十年过去了，杰克成了一个自由人，而女性再次被杀害。奥古斯特·申纳确信他是罪魁祸首。他向警方转达了一条消息，最终传到了局长马克斯·埃德尔巴赫那里。埃德尔巴赫局长认为这条线索听起来极不可能，但由于他没有其他可信的嫌疑人，他决定对杰克·翁特韦格实施监视，以防万一。

50
00:47:06.000 --> 00:48:15.000
Jack led a somewhat lavish lifestyle. He often dined at cafes and restaurants with high-profile people. The rest of the time, he holed up in his high-end apartment and worked on his writing. The more Chief Edelbacher observed, the less he believed such a man could be his murderer. On June 10, 1991, Jack Unterweger paid another visit to Chief Edelbacher's office to tell him he was going to Los Angeles for five weeks to write about crime, the sex work industry, and law enforcement. He asked if the chief had any connections in the LAPD who could help him. Chief Edelbacher did not tell Jack that he was being looked at as a person of interest in the Vienna Woods crimes. Because he didn't consider Jack a likely suspect, he had no problem with him travelling to the USA. Jack Unterweger thoroughly enjoyed his time in Los Angeles.
杰克过着有些奢华的生活。他经常与名流在高档咖啡馆和餐厅用餐。其余时间，他则躲在自己高档的公寓里写作。埃德尔巴赫局长观察得越多，就越不相信这样一个人会是凶手。1991年6月10日，杰克·翁特韦格再次拜访了埃德尔巴赫局长的办公室，告诉他自己要去洛杉矶呆五周，以撰写关于犯罪、性工作产业和执法的文章。他询问局长在洛杉矶警察局是否有可以帮到他的关系。埃德尔巴赫局长并没有告诉杰克他已被视为维也纳森林案件的重点排查对象。由于他不认为杰克是重大嫌疑人，他对于杰克前往美国旅行没有任何异议。杰克·翁特韦格在洛杉矶度过了一段非常愉快的时光。

51
00:48:15.000 --> 00:49:26.000
The morning after Shannon Exley was killed, he went sightseeing and unsuccessfully tried to track down various celebrities to interview, including Cher and Zha-Zha Gabor. He got amongst it at the Gay and Lesbian Pride Parade, and a few days after Irene Rodriguez was killed, he saw the sights of Santa Monica. Early one morning, Jack left his room at the Cecil Hotel and strolled the five-minute walk to the LAPD Central Community Police Station. Flashing his ID, he explained what he was doing in the city. When he was offered the chance to go on a ride along with a local patrol officer, Jack leapt at the opportunity. The patrol officer found the small Austrian man quirky but friendly enough. He was extremely interested in Los Angeles law enforcement and constantly asked questions as he snapped photos out of the car window. A few days later, Jack returned to the police station and flirted with the female patrol officers, taking pictures of them.
香农·埃克斯利（Shannon Exley）被杀的第二天，他去观光，并试图寻找不同的名人进行采访，包括雪儿（Cher）和莎莎·嘉宝（Zha-Zha Gabor），但没有成功。他融入了同性恋骄傲大游行，在艾琳·罗德里格斯（Irene Rodriguez）被杀几天后，他观赏了圣莫尼卡的风景。一天清早，杰克离开卡塞尔酒店的房间，步行五分钟来到了洛杉矶警察局中央社区警察分局。他闪了一下身份证，解释了自己在这个城市的所作所为。当他获得与当地巡警一同出警的机会时，杰克欣然抓住了这个机会。巡警觉得这个身材矮小的奥地利人有点古怪，但还算友好。他对洛杉矶执法部门非常感兴趣，一边把着车窗拍照，一边不断地提问。几天后，杰克回到警察局，调戏女巡警并给她们拍照。

52
00:49:26.000 --> 00:50:45.000
Soon after, the third American sex worker, Peggy Booth, was murdered. Upon his return to Austria, Jack Unterweger met with Chief Edelbacher to discuss what he'd learned about sex work and crime in Los Angeles. As they chatted, Chief Edelbacher admitted to Jack that he was a person of interest in the Vienna Woods murders. Jack wasn't surprised, commenting that his background made him an obvious target while reassuring the Chief that he was in no way responsible. Nevertheless, Chief Edelbacher asked Jack to provide alibis for the nights that the murdered women had disappeared. He agreed and promised to do so within two weeks. But soon enough, Chief Edelbacher received a statement from Jack Unterweger saying he couldn't give any alibis for the nights in question as he couldn't remember what he was doing. Meanwhile, almost 200 kilometres south in the Austrian city of Graz, detectives began to suspect that two unsolved murders they were investigating were linked to the Vienna Woods crimes.
不久之后，第三名美国性工作者佩吉·布斯（Peggy Booth）遇害。回到奥地利后，杰克·翁特韦格会见了埃德尔巴赫局长，讨论了他对洛杉矶性工作和犯罪的了解。在他们聊天时，埃德尔巴赫局长向杰克承认，他是维也纳森林谋杀案的重点排查对象。杰克并不感到惊讶，评论说他的背景使他成为了显而易见的靶子，同时向局长保证他绝对没有责任。尽管如此，埃德尔巴赫局长还是要求杰克为受害女性失踪的那些夜晚提供不在场证明。他同意了，并承诺在两周内提供。但不久之后，埃德尔巴赫局长收到了一份来自杰克·翁特韦格的声明，称他无法为相关夜晚提供任何不在场证明，因为他不记得自己当时在做什么。与此同时，在向南约200公里的奥地利城市格拉茨，侦探们开始怀疑他们正在调查的两起未破谋杀案与维也纳森林案件有关。

53
00:50:45.000 --> 00:51:55.000
On the night of October 26, 1990, Brunhilde Masseur was standing on her regular corner in Graz's red light district. As the nearby clock tower illuminated the time of 12.15am, a taxi driver who knew Brunhilde pulled over to ask why she was out so late. Brunhilde explained that she was hoping for one last customer before heading home. She planned to take her children on an outing in the morning and wanted a bit more spending money for them. The taxi driver bid Brunhilde farewell, then continued on his way. Brunhilde never made it home that night. Two months later in January 1991, some children playing in a wooded area on the outskirts of the city came across Brunhilde's body. She was lying in a shallow brook, naked, face down, and poorly concealed by a few tree branches. Her clothing and purse had been taken, but she was still wearing her jewellery.
1990年10月26日晚，布伦希尔德·马瑟（Brunhilde Masseur）正站在格拉茨红灯区她固定的街角。当附近钟楼的时钟显示凌晨12点15分时，一名认识布伦希尔德的出租车司机把车停在路边，询问她为什么这么晚还在外面。布伦希尔德解释说，她在回家前希望能做成最后一单生意。她计划早上带孩子们去游玩，想为他们多攒点零花钱。出租车司机向布伦希尔德道别，然后继续上路了。布伦希尔德那天晚上再也没有回家。两个月后的1991年1月，一些在城市郊区树林里玩耍的孩子偶然发现了布伦希尔德的尸体。她躺在一个浅浅的小溪里，赤身裸体，面朝下，被几根树枝草草掩盖。她的衣服和钱包被拿走了，但她还戴着首饰。

54
00:51:55.000 --> 00:53:12.000
She had been stabbed once in the buttock and a piece of fabric was not untightly around her neck. Due to the advanced state of decomposition, the forensic pathologist could not determine what the fabric was. Then, on March 7, 1991, 35-year-old sex worker Alfreda Schrempf also vanished from Graz without a trace. It would be another seven months before her skeletal remains were found not far from where Brunhilde had been dumped. She was face down and naked aside from a pair of red socks. Alfreda's cause of death couldn't be determined, but strangulation seemed most likely given there were no other signs of fatal injury, such as bullet, knife, or blunt force trauma. Despite their best efforts, investigators in Graz hadn't been able to find the person responsible for these crimes. But they noticed they bore striking similarities to another unsolved murder that had been committed late the previous year on the other side of the country.
她的臀部被刺了一刀，脖子上松松地系着一块布。由于尸体腐烂严重，法医病理学家无法确定那块布是什么。接着，在1991年3月7日，35岁的性工作者阿尔弗雷达·施雷姆普夫（Alfreda Schrempf）也在格拉茨离奇失踪，没有留下任何痕迹。又过了七个月，人们在离布伦希尔德被抛尸不远的地方发现了她的骸骨。她面朝下，除了穿着一双红袜子外一丝不挂。阿尔弗雷达的死因无法确定，但鉴于没有致命伤（如枪伤、刀伤或钝器创伤）的其他迹象，勒死似乎是最有可能的原因。尽管格拉茨的调查人员尽了最大努力，却一直未能找到对这些罪行负责的人。但他们注意到，这些案件与去年年底在全国另一端发生的另一起未破谋杀案有着惊人的相似之处。

55
00:53:12.000 --> 00:54:09.000
31-year-old sex worker Heidi Hammerer had vanished from the Austrian city of Bregens on the night of December 5, 1990. She'd been spotted at 9.30pm standing on her regular corner near Bregens train station. A few hours later, a neighbour saw Heidi back at home in her apartment garage. She was with a short man who wore a red scarf and a beige leather jacket. That was the last confirmed sighting of her. Just over three weeks later on New Year's Eve, two hikers traversing the nearby Lüstenauer Marsch found Heidi's body. She was lying face down and almost fully clothed with her petticoat shoved down her throat. Her wrists showed restraint marks, but there was no evidence that a sexual assault had taken place.
31岁的性工作者海蒂·哈默雷尔（Heidi Hammerer）于1990年12月5日晚从奥地利城市布雷根茨失踪。晚上9点30分，有人看到她站在布雷根茨火车站附近的固定街角。几个小时后，一位邻居看到海蒂回到了她位于公寓的车库里。她和一个身材矮小、戴着红围巾、穿着米色皮夹克的人在一起。那是最后一次有人确信看到她。仅仅三周多后的除夕夜，两名穿越附近吕斯特瑙沼泽（Lüstenauer Marsch）的徒步者发现了海蒂的尸体。她面朝下躺着，几乎穿戴整齐，衬裙被塞进了喉咙里。她的手腕上有被拘禁的痕迹，但没有发生性侵犯的证据。

56
00:54:09.000 --> 00:55:09.000
Her pantyhose were tied around her neck in a series of tight and intricate knots. And this time, the killer had left evidence behind. Red and black fibres on Heidi's clothing had likely come from something her assailant was wearing. When bodies started turning up throughout the Vienna woods, investigators in Graz noted how similar the crimes were to their own unsolved cases. The way the victims had been found and the method of killing was almost identical. When they found out that their colleagues in Vienna had looked into Jack Unterweger as a person of interest, they began digging into his whereabouts at the time of each murder. Hours before Alfreda Schrempf disappeared from Graz, Jack Unterweger was in the nearby town of Kufla for a reading in a local cafe.
她的连裤袜在脖子上打了一系列紧密而复杂的结。这一次，凶手留下了证据。海蒂衣服上的红黑纤维很可能是她袭击者穿着的衣物上的。当维也纳森林各处开始出现尸体时，格拉茨的调查人员注意到这些罪行与他们自己的未破案件是多么相似。受害者的发现方式和杀害手段几乎完全一致。当他们发现维也纳的同事已经将杰克·翁特韦格列为重点排查对象时，他们开始深入挖掘他在每起谋杀案发生时的行踪。在阿尔弗雷达·施雷姆普夫从格拉茨失踪前几小时，杰克·翁特韦格正在附近的库弗拉（Kufla）镇的一家当地咖啡馆里进行朗诵。

57
00:55:09.000 --> 00:56:25.000
Members of the public who had come to hear him enjoyed watching Jack's soulful performance. As the event drew to a close at 10.30pm, Jack left Kufla and headed into Graz's red light district. The night that Heidi Hammerer vanished, a white vehicle with the Vienna number plate W. Jack 1 was spotted driving past the train station she stood near. Another sex worker said she had actually seen Jack Unterweger approach Heidi before she went missing. The next day, he recorded a performance of his play Dungeon at the Austrian Broadcasting Corporation Studios, just eight miles south of Heidi's apartment. Gradually, the Graz detectives pieced together a timeline proving that each time a sex worker went missing, Jack had been attending a book signing or was working nearby. Although he insisted that he had no contact with sex workers outside of his research, a woman came forward with a different story. She had been picked up by Jack Unterweger on October 17, 1990.
前来聆听的公众非常欣赏杰克充满深情的表演。随着活动在晚上10点30分接近尾声，杰克离开库弗拉，前往格拉茨的红灯区。在海蒂·哈默雷尔失踪的那天晚上，一辆挂着维也纳车牌W. Jack 1的白色汽车被拍到从她站立的火车站附近驶过。另一名性工作者称，她在海蒂失踪前确实看到杰克·翁特韦格走近海蒂。第二天，他在奥地利广播公司录音室录制了他的戏剧《地牢》的演出，该录音室位于海蒂公寓正南方仅八英里处。格拉茨的侦探们逐渐拼凑出一条时间线，证明每次有性工作者失踪时，杰克要么在参加新书签售会，要么就在附近工作。尽管他坚称自己除了研究之外没有与性工作者接触过，但一名女性出面讲述了一个不同的故事。她于1990年10月17日被杰克·翁特韦格接上车。

58
00:56:25.000 --> 00:57:15.000
Not long after she entered his car, he drove her to some nearby woods and cuffed her, then began violently raping her. Frightened, the woman began to cry. This seemed to spur Jack on. When he was unable to ejaculate, he angrily released the woman before driving off. The incident had traumatized the sex worker, leaving her terrified ever since. When Jack learnt of this woman's statement, he changed his story. Now he admitted that he had picked up a sex worker once, but it was entirely consensual. The handcuffs were nothing more than a birthday gift from a friend that he had stashed in his car's glove box.
她上车不久后，他把她开车带到附近的树林里，给她戴上手铐，然后开始暴力强奸她。受惊的女子哭了起来。这似乎更加刺激了杰克。当他无法射精时，他愤怒地释放了这名女子，然后开车离去。这起事件对这名性工作者造成了心理创伤，让她此后一直生活在恐惧中。当杰克得知这名女性的陈述时，他改变了说辞。现在他承认自己确实接载过一次性工作者，但完全是双方自愿的。手铐不过是一个朋友送的生日礼物，他把它藏在汽车的手套箱里。

59
00:57:15.000 --> 00:58:07.000
And suddenly, Jack claimed that he remembered what he had done on the night that one victim went missing. He'd been with a girlfriend in Vienna. Investigators knew this wasn't true. Jack had been seen by a large number of people at a poetry reading on the night in question. This outright lie convinced Austrian authorities that Jack Unterweger could indeed be the murderer they were looking for. He was placed under surveillance once again. As part of the investigation, authorities began looking into unsolved murders of sex workers in other European countries. They discovered that when Jack Unterweger had been in Prague for work in September of 1990,
突然之间，杰克声称他想起了自己在一个受害者失踪的那天晚上做了什么。他在维也纳和一个女朋友在一起。调查人员知道这不是真的。在事发当晚的诗歌朗诵会上，杰克被大量的人看到过。这个公然的谎言使奥地利当局确信，杰克·翁特韦格确实可能是他们要找的凶手。他再次被置于监视之下。作为调查的一部分，当局开始调查欧洲其他国家发生的性工作者未破谋杀案。他们发现，当杰克·翁特韦格于1990年9月因工作在布拉格时——

60
00:58:07.000 --> 00:59:05.000
four months after his release from prison, a young woman named Blanka Bukova disappeared from the city after leaving a café. Blanka's body was discovered the next day in a nearby forest. She was naked and lying face down with a few sticks and twigs scattered across her body. Blanka had been stabbed once on one of her buttocks and then strangled to death with an unknown ligature which wasn't at the crime scene. Investigators' suspicions that Jack Unterweger was responsible only increased when the landlady of the hotel he'd been staying at reported seeing him in the same city square where Blanka was last seen. At around the same time that she vanished. Despite the increasing circumstantial evidence against Jack Unterweger, Vienna's district attorney concluded there wasn't enough to warrant an arrest.
就在他出狱四个月后——一个名叫布兰卡·布科娃（Blanka Bukova）的年轻女性在离开一家咖啡馆后从该市失踪。第二天，布兰卡尸体在附近的森林里被发现。她赤身裸体、面朝下躺着，尸体上散落着几根树枝和细枝。布兰卡的臀部被刺了一刀，然后被一件不在犯罪现场的未知勒索物勒死。当杰克住过的酒店的女房东报告说看到他在布兰卡最后一次被看到的同一个城市广场出现时，调查人员对杰克·翁特韦格是罪魁祸首的怀疑进一步加深了。大约就在她失踪的时候。尽管针对杰克·翁特韦格的间接证据不断增加，但维也纳地区检察官得出结论，认为证据还不足以发出逮捕令。

61
00:59:05.000 --> 01:00:11.000
The district attorney in Graz disagreed and on February 13, 1992, he successfully petitioned the Graz criminal court to order Jack's arrest. Two days later, investigators rushed to Jack's apartment to apprehend him armed with an arrest warrant, but he wasn't at home. Detectives began rummaging through the residence. It was spotlessly clean with nothing out of place. However, a search soon uncovered three pairs of handcuffs, a can of pepper spray, a switchblade knife and a shotgun. As a convicted felon, Jack was not permitted to own any of these items. Detectives also found a beige leather jacket, similar to the one described by a witness who had seen Heidi Hammerer with a short man on the night of her murder. A red scarf seemed similar to the fibers found on Heidi's clothing.
格拉茨的地区检察官则持不同意见，并于1992年2月13日成功请求格拉茨刑事法院下令逮捕杰克。两天后，调查人员带着逮捕令冲进杰克的公寓捉拿他，但他不在家。侦探们开始在住所内搜翻。这里一尘不染，没有一样东西摆错位置。然而，搜查很快发现了三副手铐、一罐胡椒喷雾、一把弹簧刀和一支猎枪。作为一名被定罪的重罪犯，杰克是不被允许拥有这些物品中的任何一件的。侦探们还找到了一件米色皮夹克，这与目击者描述在谋杀案当晚看到海蒂·翁特韦格和一个身材矮小的人在一起时穿的夹克相似。一条红围巾似乎与在海蒂衣服上发现的纤维相似。

62
01:00:11.000 --> 01:01:16.000
Discovered in Jack's library was a collection of books and manuscripts that featured the same unusual words used in prank calls to Rudolph Pram. Hades, the Atonement, Zenith and references to the figure eight. When investigators eventually learned about the prank calls, they struggled to determine the meaning behind these strange phrases. One possible explanation behind the reference to the figure eight was that this was the shape a restraint made when tying someone's hands behind their back. Another remark from the calls that puzzled detectives was the killer's claim, quote, To eleven, I have carried out the just punishment. Jack Unterweger was suspected of murdering seven women in Austria and one in Prague throughout the year following his release. Investigators wondered if there were three more murders they were unaware of.
在杰克的书房里发现了一系列书籍和手稿，里面带有在给鲁道夫·普拉姆的恶作剧电话中使用的那些不同寻常的词汇。“哈迪斯”、“救赎”、“极点”以及对数字“八”的引用。当调查人员最终了解到这些恶作剧电话时，他们费力地揣摩这些奇怪短语背后的含义。对数字“八”的引用的一个可能解释是，这是将某人的双手反绑在背后时，束缚物所形成的形状。侦探们感到困惑的电话中的另一个言论是凶手的声称，引述：“对于十一个，我已经执行了正义的惩罚。”杰克·翁特韦格被怀疑在出狱后的这一年中，在奥地利谋杀了七名女性，在布拉格谋杀了另一名女性。调查人员想知道是否还有他们不知道的三起谋杀案。

